## Ingredients

Use what you have on hand.
Great for leftover ingredients

- [ ] 1/2 stick [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" } or 1 Tbsp olive or vegetable oil
- [ ] (Optional) 1.5 cups fingerling or [yukon gold potatoes]{ ing="yukon-gold-potatoes" }, steamed until tender then cut into 1/2” dice (or cubed then microwaved for 4-6 min)

      - [ ] [sweet]{ ing="sweet" }, white, or yellow potatoes or winter squash
      - [ ] couscous and [rice also work]{ ing="rice-also-work" }
- [ ] (Optional) 1 cup (2 ounces) [button mushrooms]{ ing="button-mushrooms" }, small dice
- [ ] (Optional) medium [red onion]{ ing="red-onion" }, small dice
- [ ] (Optional) [red bell pepper]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" }, small dice
- [ ] (Optional) [broccoli]{ ing="broccoli" }, asparagus, carrot, etc.
- [ ] [salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }
- [ ] (Optional) 1/8 teaspoon [finely grated lemon zest]{ ing="finely-grated-lemon-zest" }
- [ ] (Optional) [paprika]{ ing="paprika" }, cinnamon, or other spices depending on ingredients
- [ ] [egg]{ ing="egg" } (fry or poach)

## Recipe

1. Ensure that all of the ingredients are pre-cooked. Vegetables can be cooked in water or broth or softened in a microwave. Make sure to cut into small cubes
1. Use a cast iron skillet to get the best crisp and heat all of the ingredients on medium-high heat until warm and slightly browned
1. Add the quicker-cooking ingredients last and cook the [egg]{ ing="egg" }.
